+---
+id: project-checks
+kind: deterministic
+command: {{INVOKE}} engine sensor-project-checks
+default_severity: advisory
+description: Runs the project's own checkers from aidlc/spaces/<space>/checkers.json on a written source file
+category: code-quality
+fire_on: write
+matches: "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts,js,jsx,mjs,cjs,py,go,rs,java,kt,kts,cs,rb,php,swift,c,cc,cpp,h,hpp,scala,sh,tf}"
+input_schema:
+  file_path: string
+output_schema:
+  pass: boolean
+  checkers:
+    - label: string
+      status: string
+  violations:
+    - checker: string
+      file: string
+      line: number
+      rule: string
+      message: string
+timeout_seconds: 120
+---
+
+# project-checks sensor
+
+Runs the checkers a project names for itself (its linter, type checker or a
+fast test command) against each source file written during a stage. The
+`linter` and `type-check` sensors guess the tool; this one runs exactly what the
+project configured.
+
+## Configuration
+
+`aidlc/spaces/<space>/checkers.json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "checkers": [
+    {
+      "label": "eslint",
+      "command": ["node_modules/.bin/eslint", "--format=json", "{file}"],
+      "matches": "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
+      "parser": "eslint",
+      "timeoutSeconds": 30
+    },
+    {
+      "label": "unit tests",
+      "command": ["bun", "test"],
+      "matches": "src/**/*.ts",
+      "parser": "exit-code",
+      "timeoutSeconds": 60
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+- `command` is an argv array, never a shell string. `{file}` is replaced by the
+  written file's path relative to the checker's working directory; without it
+  the command checks the whole project. `node_modules/.bin` and `.venv/bin`
+  under the working directory are searched before `PATH`.
+- `cwd` (optional) is a project-relative working directory.
+- `matches` (optional, default every file) is a project-relative glob.
+- `parser` reads the output: `eslint` (`--format=json`), `ruff`
+  (`--output-format=json`), `generic` (`file:line:col: severity: message` lines
+  and `tsc --pretty false` output) or `exit-code` (a non-zero exit is a finding
+  carrying the output's last lines).
+- `timeoutSeconds` defaults to 30; all checkers share the sensor's 120-second
+  budget.
+
+Without the file, or when no checker matches the written file, the sensor
+passes with `Note=tool-unavailable`. A malformed file is a script error, so the
+fix is visible in the audit without failing writes.
+
+## Failure mode
+
+Emits `SENSOR_FAILED` when a checker reports an error-severity finding, and
+writes detail to
+`aidlc/spaces/<active-space>/intents/<active-intent>/.aidlc-engine/sensors/<stage-slug>/project-checks-<fire-id>.md`
+with each finding's checker, file, line, rule and message. Warnings are listed
+but do not fail. A checker whose executable is missing is skipped and one that
+times out is reported in `checkers`; neither fails the fire.
